+HANDOFF — certificate generator for concrete circuit-size steps (founder via Claude, 2026-11-25 ~06:10Z)
+
+WHY: the audit's P0. Competitors win the concrete lower-bound family ("Table 2: ... at least K gates",
+"Graph t5-...", "False: ..." twins) with the public frontier-search engine `lb_cert` (L_meta_7281,
+Apache-2.0) plus a generator. We now have our own generator. Validated end to end with the official
+tools/check-lean.mjs: L_meta_7309 (merged instance), 5459, 8493, 8487 all ACCEPTED (check).
+We still lost those races (PRs by others at 05:45-06:03) because each local verification took ~10 min.
+LESSON: the generator is proven; DO NOT re-verify locally. Submit the moment a step is held.
+
+TOOLS (billy-dev /home/lubko/pnp-work/infra/lbgen, mirror on marceline-dev /home/lubko/pnp-infra/lbgen):
+* lbparse.py  — classifies `∀ t, HasCircuitSize n f t → K ≤ t` and `¬HasCircuitSize n f S` in any
+  pretty-printing style (elaborated `(x1 : Fin (8 : ℕ) → Bool)` binders, `.any` edge lists via a Lean
+  #eval fallback on marceline-dev). Twins are `¬ (` + LB + `)`.
+* lbgen.py    — mirrors the engine's `next`/`via`/`stepOK` exactly; decides the bound (LB_TRUE, or
+  Feasible = a (K-1)-gate circuit exists = the twin is true) and emits the certificate.
+* lbassemble.py ENGINE MODULE STMT OUT [--maxstates N] [--chunks 40] — full candidate file.
+  Compact encoding (hex wire dictionary, keys written once via List.zip, short BT aliases) is 5-10x
+  smaller than willakone's. Theorem is `:= by exact lb_cert ...` (town validator needs `by`).
+  Size limits for n = 8: ~2.8k states -> 352 KB, ~4.4k states with engine7281.pruned.lean.
+  Memory: the checker peaks at 13-23 GB for these files; --chunks 40 halves the build peak.
+* engine7281.lean = upstream L_meta_7281.lean cut before `def L_ : List ℕ :=`;
+  engine7281.pruned.lean = prune_engine.py output (57 KB; pruned variant compiles, full check of
+  8483 running at the time of writing).
+* autosolve.py (RUNNING, pid in `pgrep -af autosolve`; stop with `touch STOP` in that directory):
+  polls the public gaps.json every 60 s, pre-generates candidates into cands/<gap>.lean
+  (status in cands/<gap>.status), and when the town holds a step with a ready candidate it calls
+  `python3 -m missions.pnp.cli submit GAP FILE` (the normal publisher path). When the town holds a
+  FALSE twin whose true lower bound has a candidate and no open PR, it runs
+  ../twin_publish.py HELD TWIN FILE (join.txt: prove the negated twin as an ordinary PR) with the
+  town's own gitctl/github/validate helpers and the same signed identity.
+* decide results (marceline-dev lbgen/decide_all.out): every Table 2 pair decided so far has the
+  lower bound TRUE and the "False:" twin false. Release held "False:" twins with
+  statement_seems_false citing the decision. K = 13-15 instances exceed 20k states: out of reach
+  for this engine (needs a stronger engine, e.g. gate elimination before the search).
+
